---
import CommitFeed from "./CommitFeed.astro";

const skillGroups = [
  { label: "Languages", skills: ["Java", "Python", "SQL", "JavaScript"] },
  { label: "APIs & Integration", skills: ["REST APIs", "HTTP", "MQs", "JSON"] },
  { label: "Databases & Data", skills: ["RDBMS", "schema design", "persistence layers", "DAO pattern", "SQLite"] },
  {
    label: "Web",
    skills: ["HTML/CSS", "Bootstrap", "Flask", "API integration", "JavaScript", "DOM manipulation"],
  },
  { label: "Testing & Quality", skills: ["JUnit", "Mockito", "unit, integration and acceptance testing", "debugging", "troubleshooting"]},
  { label: "Practices", skills: ["Agile/Scrum", "code reviews", "working with existing codebases", "documentation"] },
  { label: "DevOps & Build", skills: ["Git", "CI/CD", "Docker", "build automation"] },
];

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<section id="about">
  <h2>a little about me :))))</h2>

  <div class="about-wrap about-wrap-skills">
    <div class="about-skills">
      {
        skillGroups.map((group) => (
          <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="skill-label">{group.label}</span>
            <ul class="skill-tags">
              {group.skills.map((skill) => (
                <li>{skill}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div class="about-photo">
      <img
        src={`${base}/images/IMG_5890.JPG`}
        alt="A photo of myself"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-wrap">
    <div class="about-photo">
      <img
        src={`${base}/images/IMG_5893.JPG`}
        alt="A photo of myself"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="about-text">
      <p>
        I used to explain the French Revolution to teenagers. Now I explain to a
        computer why two services won't talk to each other, genuinely not that
        different a job. Turns out that teaching maps onto software better than
        you'd think: explaining a confusing concept five different ways until it
        clicks is basically what debugging feels like to me now.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work mostly in Java, building service-oriented systems: REST APIs that
        let services talk to each other, ActiveMQ queues that let them do it
        asynchronously, and a SQLite/DAO-backed layer underneath to persist it
        all. I like the kind of problem where a few small, well-designed pieces
        have to cooperate to do something bigger than any one of them could
        alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of code, I'm probably reading about history, out hiking, or chasing a new hobby to see if it sticks.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-extras">
    <CommitFeed />
  </div>
</section>